---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Web Modernization, AI Content Ops & Digital Strategy | Guiding Point Consulting"
  description="Guiding Point Consulting delivers website modernization, AI content systems, team training, custom chatbots, and fractional digital strategy for government prime contractors and mission-based nonprofits."
>
  <!-- Page Header -->
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container hero-content">
      <h1>Services</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Five ways to work together — whether you need to modernize a website, build AI content systems, train your team, add a custom AI assistant, or lead a complex digital initiative.</p>
      <p class="hero-subtext">Guiding Point partners with government prime contractors as a trusted subcontractor and works directly with mission-based nonprofits. Either way, the work is practical, human-centered, and built to last beyond the engagement.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who We Work With -->
  <section class="who-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Who We Work With</h2>
      <div class="who-grid">
        <div class="who-card who-card--primary">
          <div class="who-badge">Primary</div>
          <h3>Government Prime Contractors</h3>
          <p class="who-label">Subcontract Support</p>
          <p>We support government primes as a qualified subcontractor delivering web modernization, AI content ops, team training, and digital strategy to the public sector clients, agencies, and communities their contracts serve. The prime stays on contract. We handle the digital and AI delivery.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="who-card">
          <div class="who-badge who-badge--secondary">Direct Engagements</div>
          <h3>Mission-Based Nonprofits</h3>
          <p>We work directly with nonprofit organizations that need clearer websites, smarter content systems, practical AI training, and custom chatbots designed for the realities of mission-driven work, limited capacity, and non-technical staff.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Services Detail -->
  <section class="services-detail">
    <div class="container">

      <!-- Service 1 -->
      <div class="service-detail-card" id="audit">
        <div class="service-badge">01</div>
        <h2>Website Audit + Modernization Roadmap</h2>
        <p class="service-tagline">Clarity on what to fix first — and a modern digital presence that works for humans and AI alike.</p>
        <div class="service-content">
          <div class="service-description">

            <div class="mod-callout">
              <p class="mod-callout-lead">Website modernization is not just a redesign.</p>
              <p>At Guiding Point, modernization means transforming your website into a clear, functional, and AI-visible digital system that supports both users and internal teams. This includes improving structure, messaging, and usability while ensuring your content is optimized for how people and AI tools discover and interact with information today.</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Who it's For</h3>
            <p>Government primes whose contracts require web modernization, accessibility, or content improvements for the organizations or communities they serve, and mission-based nonprofits that need clarity on what to fix before investing in a rebuild.</p>

            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>UX and content structure review covering clarity, navigation, and messaging for real users trying to complete real tasks.</li>
              <li>Performance and accessibility quick wins that support trust, compliance, and reduced day-to-day friction.</li>
              <li>SEO fundamentals check including metadata, indexability, and on-page issues.</li>
              <li>AEO (Answer Engine Optimization) and GEO (Generative Engine Optimization) so your content is discoverable by both search engines and AI tools.</li>
              <li>Conversion review covering CTAs, flow, and friction points.</li>
              <li>A prioritized roadmap from quick wins to larger upgrades with effort and impact notes your leadership and technical teams can actually use.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="mod-columns">
              <div class="mod-col">
                <h4>What This Is</h4>
                <ul class="mod-list mod-list--is">
                  <li>A structured modernization of your digital presence</li>
                  <li>A system your team can manage after we leave</li>
                  <li>A platform optimized for both human users and AI-driven discovery</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="mod-col">
                <h4>What This Is Not</h4>
                <ul class="mod-list mod-list--not">
                  <li>A visual-only redesign</li>
                  <li>A branding-only exercise</li>
                  <li>A one-time build with no internal systems</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Outcome</h3>
            <p>A practical, sequenced plan — and a website that is usable, discoverable, and sustainable in an AI-driven digital environment. You can execute with us, your internal team, or existing vendors without guessing where to start.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="service-cta">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Request a Consult</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Service 2 -->
      <div class="service-detail-card" id="content-ops">
        <div class="service-badge">02</div>
        <h2>AI-Supported Content Operations</h2>
        <p class="service-tagline">SOPs, prompts, QA, and workflows that help real humans ship better content, faster.</p>
        <div class="service-content">
          <div class="service-description">
            <h3>Who it's For</h3>
            <p>Government primes whose client organizations need documented AI-assisted content systems as part of a digital modernization contract, and nonprofit communications, program, and operations staff who need repeatable, staff-friendly content workflows.</p>
            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Content workflow mapping covering roles, approvals, and publishing cadence.</li>
              <li>Simple SOPs for drafting, editing, publishing, and repurposing.</li>
              <li>A prompt and template library tailored to your brand voice, audiences, and channels.</li>
              <li>QA checklist for facts, tone, accessibility, and compliance-friendly checks.</li>
              <li>Templates for briefs, outlines, and production-ready drafts.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Outcome</h3>
            <p>A repeatable content system that helps your team publish faster and stay aligned without bottlenecks or guesswork.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="service-cta">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Build Content Ops</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Service 3 -->
      <div class="service-detail-card" id="ai-training">
        <div class="service-badge">03</div>
        <h2>AI Team Training</h2>
        <p class="service-tagline">Help your staff use AI safely and confidently in their day-to-day work.</p>
        <div class="service-content">
          <div class="service-description">
            <h3>Who it's For</h3>
            <p>Government primes who need qualified subcontract support to deliver AI literacy and adoption training to the organizations their contracts serve, and nonprofit teams whose staff are using AI inconsistently or not at all.</p>
            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Plain-language training on what AI can and cannot do.</li>
              <li>Role-based examples for program, comms, development, and operations staff.</li>
              <li>Guardrails for privacy, compliance, and brand voice.</li>
              <li>Guided practice using your own content, templates, and prompt kits.</li>
              <li>Simple decision points for when to use AI and when not to, written so non-technical staff can follow them.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Outcome</h3>
            <p>A team that knows how to use AI with confidence, consistency, and appropriate caution — built around your actual tools and workflows.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="service-cta">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Schedule a Training</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Service 4 -->
      <div class="service-detail-card" id="chatbots">
        <div class="service-badge">04</div>
        <h2>Custom Mission-Aware Chatbots and AI Assistants</h2>
        <p class="service-tagline">AI built from your own content, in your own voice, designed for the people you serve.</p>
        <div class="service-content">
          <div class="service-description">
            <h3>Who it's For</h3>
            <p>Government primes whose contracts include AI tool implementation or digital capacity building for client organizations, and nonprofits ready to give staff and visitors a faster, more accurate way to find answers and content support.</p>
            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A custom AI assistant trained on your FAQs, website content, and key documents.</li>
              <li>Client and visitor-facing support for common questions without burdening staff.</li>
              <li>Internal staff support for quickly locating policies, procedures, and reference language.</li>
              <li>On-brand content starting points grounded in your actual programs and services.</li>
              <li>Full documentation so you own the configuration, prompts, and knowledge base with no vendor lock-in.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Outcome</h3>
            <p>A chatbot that sounds like your organization, understands your work, and reduces repetitive load on your team without feeling like a generic widget.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="service-cta">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Explore a Custom Chatbot</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Service 5 -->
      <div class="service-detail-card" id="strategy">
        <div class="service-badge">05</div>
        <h2>Fractional Digital Strategy Lead</h2>
        <p class="service-tagline">A steady partner who keeps projects moving and conversations grounded in reality.</p>
        <div class="service-content">
          <div class="service-description">
            <h3>Who it's For</h3>
            <p>Government primes who need a reliable subcontract digital strategy partner to lead web, content, and AI workstreams for the organizations their contracts serve, and nonprofit leaders who need ongoing senior digital guidance without adding a full-time role.</p>
            <h3>What You Get</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Weekly or biweekly strategy and priority alignment.</li>
              <li>Roadmap management covering what ships next, what matters most, and what pauses.</li>
              <li>Stakeholder coordination across leadership, program and marketing, and technical and creative teams.</li>
              <li>Performance tracking and iteration loops tied to the metrics that matter to you.</li>
              <li>Guardrails for brand consistency, content quality, and responsible AI use.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Outcome</h3>
            <p>Momentum, clarity, and measurable progress with one point of contact who keeps people, timelines, and decisions moving.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="service-cta">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Discuss a Retainer</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Not Sure CTA -->
  <section class="not-sure-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="not-sure-content">
        <h2>Not sure which fits? Or are you a prime looking for subcontract support?</h2>
        <p>Send a quick note about your project, contract, or organization and we will recommend the best starting point. No pressure, no hard sell.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Page Header ─────────────────────────────── */
  .page-header {
    background: var(--white);
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0 var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
  }

  .hero-content {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .hero-text {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-md);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--gray-600);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .hero-subtext {
    max-width: 750px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--gray-500);
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ── Who We Work With ────────────────────────── */
  .who-section {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0 var(--space-xl);
    background: var(--off-white);
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    color: var(--indigo);
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .who-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .who-card {
    background: var(--white);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 2px solid var(--gray-200);
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
    position: relative;
  }

  .who-card--primary {
    border-color: var(--rust);
    background: rgba(172, 52, 48, 0.03);
  }

  .who-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--rust);
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(172, 52, 48, 0.1);
  }

  .who-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    background: rgba(172, 52, 48, 0.1);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 20px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .who-badge--secondary {
    color: var(--indigo);
    background: rgba(50, 52, 90, 0.08);
  }

  .who-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--indigo);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .who-label {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--rust);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .who-card p {
    color: var(--gray-700);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* ── Services Detail ─────────────────────────── */
  .services-detail {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0;
  }

  .service-detail-card {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-3xl);
    padding: var(--space-2xl);
    background: var(--gray-50);
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
  }

  .service-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--rust);
    color: white;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .service-detail-card h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 2.5rem;
  }

  .service-tagline {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gray-600);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .service-content {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .service-description h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--indigo);
  }

  .service-description h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .service-description h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--indigo);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .service-description ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .service-description li {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .service-description li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  /* ── Modernization Callout (Service 01) ──────── */
  .mod-callout {
    background: rgba(50, 52, 90, 0.04);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--indigo);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .mod-callout-lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--indigo);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .mod-callout p {
    color: var(--gray-700);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .mod-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--white);
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
  }

  .mod-col h4 {
    color: var(--indigo);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .mod-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .mod-list li {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    position: relative;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .mod-list--is li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--indigo);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Override the default ✓ bullet for mod-list--is */
  .mod-list--is li,
  .mod-list--not li {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .mod-list--is li::before,
  .mod-list--not li::before {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
  }

  .mod-list--not li::before {
    content: '✕';
    color: var(--gray-500);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ── Service CTA ─────────────────────────────── */
  .service-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
  }

  /* ── Not Sure Section ────────────────────────── */
  .not-sure-section {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(172, 52, 48, 0.05) 0%, rgba(50, 52, 90, 0.05) 100%);
  }

  .not-sure-content {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .not-sure-content h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .not-sure-content p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* ── Buttons ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.875rem 2rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    cursor: pointer;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--rust);
    color: var(--white);
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: #8b2a26;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(172, 52, 48, 0.3);
  }

  /* ── Responsive ──────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .service-detail-card {
      padding: var(--space-lg);
    }

    .service-detail-card h2 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .who-grid,
    .mod-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>